{"id":"word:hebrew:H3658","type":"word","title":"כִּנּוֹר","subtitle":"H3658 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a harp","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כִּנּוֹר (H3658) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 42 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כִּנּוֹר (kinnôwr) means a harp First listed occurrence: 1Chr 13 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כִּנּוֹר","transliteration":"kinnôwr","pronunciation":"kin-nore'","strong":"H3658","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3658","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בְּ/כִנֹּר֥וֹת","וּ/בְ/כִנֹּר֔וֹת","וְ/כִנֹּר֔וֹת","וְ/כִנֹּר֥וֹת","כִּנּ֖וֹר"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsa",8],["HC/R/Ncmpa",7],["HC/Ncmpa",6],["HC/Ncmsa",6],["HNcmsa",5],["HRd/Ncmsa",3],["HR/Ncmpa",2],["HTd/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmpc/Sp2fs",1],["HC/R/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a harp","usage":"harp.","full":"H3658. kinnor כִּנּוֺר noun masculine Psa 81:3 lyre (on formation compare Lag BN 89, Anm .; Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic כִּנָּרָא , ; Mandean כינאר(אׅ Nö M § 104 (who questions Shemitic origin); Arabic , ; as loan-word in Hellen. Greek κινύρα ( ᵐ5 and Joseph.); in Egyptian kn-an-aul according to Bondi 79 ) — absolute ׳כ Gen 4:21 +; suffix כִּנֹּרִי Job 30:31 ; plural כִּנֹּרוֺת 1Kin 10:12 +; suffix כִּנּוֺרַיִךְ Ezek 26:13 , כִּנֹּרוֺתֵינוּ Psa 137:2 ; &#8212; lyre , stringed instrument used for popular as well as sacred music (compare Benz Archaeology 273 ff. Now Archaeology i. 273 ff. ); — ׳יְעוּגָבכ Gen 4:21 , וּבְכ ׳בְּתֹף 31:27 ; בַּכּ מְנַגֵּן יֹדֵעַ ׳אִישׁ 1Sam 16:16 a man skilled in playing on the lyre , compare 16:23 ( בְּיָדוֺׅ וִנִגֵּן ); at banquets Isa 5:12 (+ חָלִיל תֹּף, נֶבֶל, ), token of merriment 24:8 (+ תֻּמִּים ), Ezek 26:13 , compare בֹּכִים לְקוֺל וְעֻגָבִי כִּנֹּרִ֑י לְאֵבֶל וַיְהִי Job 30:31 , וְכ כְתֹף ׳יִשְׂאוּ עוּגָב לְקוֺל וְיִשְׂמְחוּ 21:12 ; carried by a loose woman Isa 23:16 (figurative of Tyre); in simile 16:11 (of murmuring sound of bowels = heart, in pity); used also in praising ׳י , usually As accompaniment of song (compare 1Chr 15:16 ) וְכ וְחָלִיל וְתֹף ׳נֵבֶל 1Sam 10:5 ; Isa 30:32 (|| תֻּמִּים ); especially before the ark 2Sam 6:5 (+ תֻּמִּים נְבָלִים, , etc.) || 1Chr 13:8 , and in sanctuary (usually + נֵבֶל , etc.) 1Kin 10:12 , but especially Chronicles, Psalms: &#8212; 1Chr 13:8 (plural, and so chiefly in Chronicles), 15:16 , 21 , 28 ; 16:5 ; 25:1 , 3 , 6 ; 2Chr 5:12 ; 9:11 ; 20:28 ; 29:25 ; Neh 12:27 ; Psa 33:2 (singular, and so chiefly in Psalms), 43:4 ; 49:5 ; 57:9 ; 71:22 ; 81:3 ; 92:4 ; 98:5 (twice in verse); 108:3 ; 147:7 ; 149:3 ; 150:3 ; compare כִּנֹּרוֺתֵינוּ 137:2 . &#8212; Vbs. used with ׳כ are: — תָּפַשׂ Gen 4:21 , בְּ נִגֵּן 1Sam 16:16 , בְּ מְשַׂחֵק 2Sam 6:5 = 1Chr 13:8 , בּ מְשֹׁרֲרִים 15:16 , בְּ מַשְׁמִיעִים 15:28 , בְּ נִבָּא 25:1 , 3 , בְּ הוֺדָה Psa 33:2 ; 43:4 , בְּ זמּר 71:22 ; 98:5 ; 147:7 ; 149:3 , בְּ הַלֲלוּהוּ 150:3 . &#8212; On ancient lyres see references in Dr Amos, p. 236 f .","rootNote":"from a unused root meaning to twang;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 13 8","keyReferences":["1Chr 13 8","1Chr 15 16","1Chr 15 21","1Chr 15 28","1Chr 16 5","1Chr 25 1","1Chr 25 3","1Chr 25 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":42,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 13 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":13,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בְ/כִנֹּרוֹת֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/כִנֹּר֖וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/כִנֹּר֥וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 28","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/כִנֹּרֽוֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmpa"},{"